## Security Recommendations

Based on the assessment, recommended security practices include:

* Keep Windows Firewall enabled.
* Maintain up-to-date endpoint protection.
* Apply security updates regularly.
* Use strong password policies.
* Enable appropriate account-lockout controls.
* Avoid unnecessary administrator privileges.
* Disable unnecessary services where appropriate.
* Maintain security auditing and event logging.
* Regularly review local accounts and permissions.
* Follow the principle of least privilege.

## Conclusion

This lab demonstrates practical Windows endpoint security hardening techniques.

The exercise provided hands-on experience with identifying security weaknesses, reviewing Windows security controls, applying appropriate configurations, and verifying the resulting security posture.

The project also demonstrates how endpoint hardening can reduce attack surface and improve the overall security of a Windows environment.

## Disclaimer

This assessment was conducted exclusively on a Windows virtual machine within an authorized and isolated personal cybersecurity laboratory. No unauthorized systems or networks were targeted.
